s","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://taylor.town/succession-000\"\u003ehttps://taylor.town/succession-000\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442699\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442699\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 138\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 141\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://taylor.town/succession-000","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442699","date_published":"2026-03-19T17:16:36Z","author":{"name":"surprisetalk","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=surprisetalk"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442690","title":"Google details new 24-hour process to sideload unverified Android apps","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://android-developers.googleblog.com/2026/03/android-developer-verification.html\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://android-developers.googleblog.com/2026/03/android-de...\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442690\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442690\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 419\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 502\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/03/google-details-new-24-hour-process-to-sideload-unverified-android-apps/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442690","date_published":"2026-03-19T17:16:04Z","author":{"name":"0xedb","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=0xedb"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442435","title":"Scaling Karpathy's Autoresearch: What Happens When the Agent Gets a GPU Cluster","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://blog.skypilot.co/scaling-autoresearch/\"\u003ehttps://blog.skypilot.co/scaling-autoresearch/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442435\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442435\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 112\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 53\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://blog.skypilot.co/scaling-autoresearch/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47442435","date_published":"2026-03-19T16:55:45Z","author":{"name":"hopechong","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=hopechong"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47441784","title":"World Happiness Report 2026","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://www.worldhappiness.report/ed/2026/\"\u003ehttps://www.worldhappiness.report/ed/2026/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47441784\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47441784\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 116\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 91\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.worldhappiness.report/ed/2026/","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47441784","date_published":"2026-03-19T16:12:48Z","author":{"name":"ChrisArchitect","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=ChrisArchitect"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47441546","title":"Show HN: Three new Kitten TTS models – smallest less than 25MB","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eKitten TTS (\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/KittenML/KittenTTS\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://github.com/KittenML/KittenTTS\u003c/a\u003e) is an open-source series of tiny and expressive text-to-speech models for on-device applications. We had a thread last year here: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44807868\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=44807868\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cp\u003eToday we're releasing three new models with 80M, 40M and 14M parameters.\u003cp\u003eThe largest model (80M) has the highest quality. The 14M variant reaches new SOTA in expressivity among similar sized models, despite being \u003c25MB in size. This release is a major upgrade from the previous one and supports English text-to-speech applications in eight voices: four male and four female.\u003cp\u003eHere's a short demo: \u003ca href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ge3u5qblqZA\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ge3u5qblqZA\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cp\u003eMost models are quantized to int8 + fp16, and they use ONNX for runtime. Our models are designed to run anywhere eg. raspberry pi, low-end smartphones, wearables, browsers etc. No GPU required! This release aims to bridge the gap between on-device and cloud models for tts applications. Multi-lingual model release is coming soon.\u003cp\u003eOn-device AI is bottlenecked by one thing: a lack of tiny models that actually perform. Our goal is to open-source more models to run production-ready voice agents and apps entirely on-device.\u003cp\u003eWe would love your feedback!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47441546\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47441546\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 294\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 97\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://github.com/KittenML/KittenTTS","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47441546","date_published":"2026-03-19T15:56:06Z","author":{"name":"rohan_joshi","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=rohan_joshi"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47440759","title":"macOS 26 breaks custom DNS settings including .internal","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eOne of those 'woke up to MacOS updates' and finding none of my dockers are reachable via dnsmasq (which I use), and low and behold, an update silently breaks custom dns resolution. Hopefully Apple will listen to the bug report I've made. Hold off on updating if you use this…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47440759\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47440759\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 306\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 157\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://gist.github.com/adamamyl/81b78eced40feae50eae7c4f3bec1f5a","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47440759","date_published":"2026-03-19T15:06:58Z","author":{"name":"adamamyl","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=adamamyl"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47440430","title":"4Chan mocks £520k fine for UK online safety breaches","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.ofcom.org.uk/online-safety/illegal-and-harmful-content/4chan-fined-450000-for-not-protecting-children-from-online-pornography\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://www.ofcom.org.uk/online-safety/illegal-and-harmful-c...\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47440430\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47440430\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 230\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 373\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c624330lg1ko","external_url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47440430","date_published":"2026-03-19T14:46:25Z","author":{"name":"mosura","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=mosura"}},{"id":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47439320","title":"OpenBSD: PF queues break the 4 Gbps barrier","content_html":"\n\u003cp\u003eArticle URL: \u003ca href=\"https://undeadly.org/cgi?action=article;sid=20260319125859\"\u003ehttps://undeadly.org/cgi?action=article;sid=20260319125859\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eComments URL: \u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47439320\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47439320\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoints: 176\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e# Comments: 54\u003c/p\u003e\n","url":"https://undeadly.org/cgi?action=a